    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q32",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\tan^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta+\\cot^2\\theta\\sin^2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "Use $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ and $\\cot\\theta=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta+\\cot^2\\theta\\sin^2\\theta&=\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}\\cos^2\\theta+\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\tan^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta+\\cot^2\\theta\\sin^2\\theta&=\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta\\\\\\tan^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta+\\cot^2\\theta\\sin^2\\theta&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q33",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2+(\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$",
          "worked": "Expanding the squares cancels the opposite cross terms.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2+(\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)^2&=2\\sin^2\\theta+2\\cos^2\\theta\\\\(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2+(\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)^2&=2(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)\\\\(\\sin\\theta+\\cos\\theta)^2+(\\sin\\theta-\\cos\\theta)^2&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q34",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta+\\tan^2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sec^2\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta+\\tan^2\\theta&=1+\\tan^2\\theta\\\\\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta+\\tan^2\\theta&=\\sec^2\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original expression requires $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q35",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{1}{1-\\cos\\theta}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{1}{1-\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{(1-\\cos\\theta)+(1+\\cos\\theta)}{(1+\\cos\\theta)(1-\\cos\\theta)}\\\\\\frac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{1}{1-\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{2}{1-\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{1}{1-\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{2}{\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}+\\frac{1}{1-\\cos\\theta}&=2\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original denominators require $\\cos\\theta\\ne\\pm1$, equivalently $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
